    "body": "<!-- Please see CONTRIBUTING.md for guidelines. -->\r\n\r\n## Environment\r\n\r\n* SuperCollider version: 3.12.1 and earlier\r\n* Operating system: macOS\r\n* Other details (Qt version, audio driver, etc.):\r\n\r\n## Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n```supercollider\r\n(\r\nServer.supernova;\r\ns.reboot;\r\n)\r\n\r\ns.dumpOSC; // optionally see OSC messages\r\n\r\n// ------------------\r\n// functional example\r\n~group = Group(); // create group\r\n~group.set(\\phase, [\\c0, \\c1]); // crash\r\n\r\n// ---------------\r\n// musical example\r\n(\r\n~proxy = ProxySpace(s);\r\n~buffer = Buffer.read(s, Platform.resourceDir +/+ \"sounds/a11wlk01-44_1.aiff\");\r\n~proxy[\\warp] = {Warp1.ar(1, ~buffer, \\phase.kr(0 ! 2)) * -12.dbamp};\r\n~proxy[\\warp].play;\r\n~proxy[\\phase] = {LFDNoise3.kr(0.3 ! 2)};\r\n)\r\n~proxy[\\warp].set(\\phase, ~proxy[\\phase]); // crash\r\n~proxy[\\warp].map(\\phase, ~proxy[\\phase]); // also crash\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Expected vs. actual behavior\r\n\r\nCalling `.set` on a group with an array containing control mapping messages crashes supernova. This works fine in scsynth.\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste error messages in entirety. Use gist if very long. -->\r\n<!-- If SC crashed, see CONTRIBUTING.md for how to make a crash report. -->\r\n",
